    "status": "draft",
    "documents_examined": 4,
    "bluebell_tested": true,
    "unresolved_ambiguities": 3,
    "documents_examined_note": "National Social Security Fund Act (Cap. 230, revised edition, 38-page scan); Local Governments (Amendment) (No. 2) Act, 2008 (12-page scan); Income Tax (Amendment) Act, 2012 (4-page scan); Excise Duty (Amendment) Act, 2024 (text-layer PDF). All four ingested end to end; the anchor scan reads 53 of the NSSF Act's body sections (section 20 is on a page the transcription lost; section 9 is the ambiguity below), 12 schedule items and the three closing schedules and 18 in the 2008 Act, and the 2008 Act's scaffold round-trips through Bluebell with no findings.",
    "ambiguities": [
      "A body section is dropped when the sentence before it names a schedule and that schedule holds an item with the section's number: in the NSSF Act, section 8 ends '... specified in Schedule 2 to this Act ...', Schedule 2 has an item 9, and '9. Cancellation of registration' is not anchored. Coverage still reads 54 of 54, because the schedule's item supplies the number.",
      "A schedule that itself divides into Parts or Divisions (as a schedule of regulations does) is not anchored, because the scan floors schedules after the last container; its Divisions nest under the body's last Part.",
      "The Statutory Instruments Supplement numbering form has not been read through the pipeline; the si class is a hypothesis from the Act hierarchy."
    ],
    "laws_africa_reference": "ulii.org publishes unofficial consolidations built by Laws.Africa; official texts are the Gazette and the revised edition."
  },
